# The shared lines, Phase 8 session 1 (Docs/Design/84 §33, §14.1): asking for more, and the answer. Move lines (no
# concept). answer.detail is a core move talk_check --coverage found answered nowhere at Phase 7; ask.detail, the
# question that makes it due (and the insertion before a request, §7.2), had no move line either, so they are written
# here as pairs, topic by topic.
#
# What a question asks isn't known to the one answering it (a move line answers any ask.detail on its topic: "Who told
# you that?", a riddle, "Fancy helping me with the shed?"), so an answer says only what is true whatever was asked:
# - on a topic with news (a claim, a price, a wagon, a ship, an event), what the teller has: where they had it
#   (#hearsay#: never "I saw it", §15.3's T3), what the topic's own facts say (#topic.where#, #topic.price#,
#   #topic.who#, #topic.ship#, world.event_words), or that there is no more (#dunno#);
# - on everyday talk, the ordinary evasions a question gets ("Oh, you know.", "Now there's a question.") and nothing
#   that claims a fact.
# A question is asked of what was said, so ask.detail lines are gated to the topic as tightly as the answers.

## Asking for more: any topic

rule s8d_ask_any
does ask.detail
say #howso#? | How so? | #bc_and_q# | #bc_go_on# | Such as? | Meaning what?

rule s8d_ask_any2
does ask.detail
say What makes you say that? | How's that, then? | And then what? | Oh? Why's that?

rule s8d_ask_who
does ask.detail
say #s8_ask# | #s8_ask# | #s8_ask# | #howso#?

rule s8d_ask_gossip
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|news|deed|life
say Who told you that? | Who says? | Since when? | Is it certain? | Where'd you hear that? | Says who, though?

rule s8d_ask_gossip_named
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=theft|wanted|prowling|promise_broken|other
say #topic.subject#? Are you sure? | #topic.subject#, though? Truly? | Does #topic.subject# know folk are saying it?

rule s8d_ask_theft
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=theft|victim
say What was taken? | Did anyone see? | Has the Watch been told? | Was much taken?

rule s8d_ask_wanted
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=wanted
say Wanted for what, though? | Have they a notice up? | Does the Watch know where #topic.they#'s gone?

rule s8d_ask_violence
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=violence
tone serious
say Is anyone badly hurt? | When was this? | Did the Watch come?

rule s8d_ask_death
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|life|news topic.claim_kind=death
tone grave
say When? | How did it happen? | Has the family been told? | Was it sudden?

rule s8d_ask_marriage
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|life|news topic.claim_kind=marriage
tone light
say Married to whom? | When was the wedding? | Was there a feast? | Who'd have thought. When?

rule s8d_ask_newcomer
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=newcomer|gossip|news topic.claim_kind=newcomer
say Where from? | What does #topic.they# do? | Staying long, is #topic.they#? | Have you met #topic.them#?

rule s8d_ask_birth
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=life|news topic.kind=birth
tone light
say A boy or a girl? | Is the mother well? | Have they named it yet?

## Asking about the road, the wagons, the ships

rule s8d_ask_bandits
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=bandits
say Whereabouts? | How many of them? | Is anyone going after them? | Which road? | Close?

rule s8d_ask_caravan
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=caravan
say From where? | Who's driving? | When, though? | What are they bringing?

rule s8d_ask_caravan_late
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=caravan topic.kind=late
say Late why? | How late? | Is it the road again?

rule s8d_ask_ships
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=ships
say Which ship? | What's she carrying? | When's she in? | Where from?

## Asking about prices, the market, the Times

rule s8d_ask_prices
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=prices|price_cause
say Since when? | How much? | Where'd you see that? | Why, though? | Dear where?

rule s8d_ask_event
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=event
say What's it about? | When's that? | Where at? | What's it mean for prices?

rule s8d_ask_times
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=times|harvest
say Bad as that? | How do you mean? | Why's that, do you think?

rule s8d_ask_festival
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=festival
tone light
say When? | Is there to be music? | Will there be dancing? | What are you wearing?

## Asking about everyday things

rule s8d_ask_work
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=work|day
say Busy, then? | Who for? | How's that going? | Much on?

rule s8d_ask_home
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=home|family|food
say Whose turn is it? | Since when? | What happened? | All of it?

rule s8d_ask_health
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=health
tone tender
say Have you seen anyone about it? | Is it bad? | Since when? | Are you eating?

rule s8d_ask_travel
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=travel|accent|land
say Where's that, then? | Far? | Ever been back? | Which way?

rule s8d_ask_story
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=memories|lore|dreams|pastimes|animals|friends|faith|season|weather|smalltalk
say Then what? | Really? Then what? | And what happened? | Truly? Go on.

## Answers on a topic with news: what the teller has, and where they had it. Saying there's no more passes nothing on
## (`asserts none`); naming the one talked of, the place or the words passes the claim again, as telling it did.

rule s8d_ans_news
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|news|deed|life|bandits|caravan|ships|prices|price_cause|event|times|harvest|newcomer|festival
say #dunno#. | #hearsay#. | That's all I have. | That's all I was told. | Don't ask me more. | Only what I've said.

rule s8d_ans_news2
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|news|deed|life|bandits|caravan|ships|prices|price_cause|event|times|harvest|newcomer|festival
say #hearsay#, mind. | I only know what was said. | Ask around. You'll hear the same. | I wasn't there, was I?

rule s8d_ans_gossip
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|deed
say Everyone's saying it. | Half the street, by now. | I had it from someone who'd know. | Don't quote me. | I'm only telling you.

rule s8d_ans_gossip_guarded
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|deed self.honesty=guarded|sly
say Never you mind who. | I'll not say where I had it. | A little bird. | Ask me no more, and I'll tell you no lies.

rule s8d_ans_gossip_frank
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime|deed self.honesty=frank
say I'll not dress it up. That's what's said. | I tell it as I heard it. No more. | I'd not have said it if I didn't credit it.

rule s8d_ans_named
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime topic.subject
say #topic.subject#, aye. That's the name I heard. | It was #topic.subject#. So they say. | That's what they're saying of #topic.subject#.

rule s8d_ans_victim
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|crime topic.victim
say From #topic.victim#, so I heard. | #topic.victim# had the worst of it. | Ask #topic.victim#, if you dare.

rule s8d_ans_said
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|news topic.said
say I'll tell you what I heard: #topic.said# | Only this: #topic.said# | Word for word, as I had it: #topic.said#

rule s8d_ans_death
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|life|news topic.claim_kind=death
tone grave
say Not long since, I think. | I don't know more than that. I didn't like to ask. | I only just heard it myself.

rule s8d_ans_marriage
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=gossip|life|news topic.claim_kind=marriage
tone light
say Only lately. | I've not heard about a feast. | Quietly, by the sound of it.

rule s8d_ans_newcomer
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=newcomer|gossip|news topic.claim_kind=newcomer
say I've not met #topic.them# yet. | Come in from the Country, I think. | Couldn't tell you yet. Give it time.

rule s8d_ans_life
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=life|news topic.kind=birth|marriage|death|loss|apprentice|succession|work|arrest
say Only lately. | A day or two back. | Not long ago. | It's fresh news.

rule s8d_ans_bandits
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=bandits
say Couldn't say how many. Enough. | Ask the carters. They know the road. | Enough to worry the wagons. | Nobody's counted them.

rule s8d_ans_bandits_where
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=bandits topic.where
say #topic.where.capitalize#, so they say. | That's what I heard: #topic.where#. | #topic.where.capitalize#. Too close.

rule s8d_ans_caravan
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan
say The carters will know better. | Ask at the yard. | I only heard it in passing.

rule s8d_ans_caravan_where
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived|due|late topic.where
say From #topic.where#. | #topic.where.capitalize#, on the long road. | All the way from #topic.where#.

rule s8d_ans_caravan_who
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan topic.who
say #topic.who# has the reins, I heard. | It's #topic.who# driving. | #topic.who#, so they say.

rule s8d_ans_caravan_why
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan topic.kind=late topic.why
say #topic.why.capitalize#, they say. | #topic.why.capitalize#. What else? | Held up by #topic.why#.

rule s8d_ans_caravan_today
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan|ships topic.when=today
say Today, if all goes well. | Some time today. | Today, they say.

rule s8d_ans_caravan_soon
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan|ships topic.when=soon
say Soon, they say. | A day or so. | Any day now.

rule s8d_ans_caravan_what
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=caravan|ships topic.what
say #topic.what.capitalize#, mostly, I heard. | #topic.what.capitalize#. That's the talk. | #topic.what.capitalize#, by the sound of it.

rule s8d_ans_ships
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=ships topic.ship
say #topic.ship.capitalize#. | #topic.ship.capitalize#, the board says. | #topic.ship.capitalize#, I think. Ask on the quay.

rule s8d_ans_prices
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=prices|price_cause
say At the stalls. Look for yourself. | At the market. Go and look. | Ask any trader. | It's on every stall.

rule s8d_ans_prices_price
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=prices|price_cause topic.price
say #topic.price.capitalize#, last I looked. | #topic.price.capitalize#. I nearly fell over. | #topic.price.capitalize#. You heard me.

rule s8d_ans_price_cause
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=price_cause|prices topic.cause_words topic.cause!=still
say #topic.cause_words.capitalize#, they say. | It's #topic.cause_words#. That's the talk. | #topic.cause_words.capitalize#. What else?

rule s8d_ans_event
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=event world.event_words
say It's #world.event_words#. So the criers say. | #world.event_words.capitalize#. Everyone's talking of it. | #world.event_words.capitalize#, at the market.

rule s8d_ans_event_when
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=event world.event_when=now
say Now. Today. Go and see. | It's on now. | Today, at the market.

rule s8d_ans_event_soon
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=event world.event_when=soon
say Soon. A day or two. | Not yet. Soon. | Any day, they say.

rule s8d_ans_times
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=times world.times_cause
say #world.times_cause.capitalize#, mostly. | Since #world.times_cause#, I'd say. | It's been so since #world.times_cause#.

rule s8d_ans_times2
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=times|harvest
say Look at the stalls. Half of them shut. | Ask any trader. | Everyone feels it.

rule s8d_ans_festival_today
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=festival topic.when=today
tone light
say Today! Didn't you know? | Today. Now. Come on! | It's today, you goose.

rule s8d_ans_festival_soon
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=festival topic.when=soon
tone light
say In a day or two. | Soon. Very soon. | Not long now.

rule s8d_ans_festival_name
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=festival here.festival
tone light
say The #here.festival#, of course. | It's the #here.festival#. | For the #here.festival#.

## Answers on everyday talk: true whatever was asked. They pass nothing on (`asserts none`): answer.detail asserts the
## topic's claim by default, and "Now there's a question." tells nobody anything.

rule s8d_ans_any
does answer.detail
asserts none
say Oh, you know. | Now there's a question. | Hard to say. | Couldn't tell you. | Let me think. | Search me.

rule s8d_ans_any2
does answer.detail
asserts none
say It's hard to put into words. | Well, you'll see. | I'll tell you another time. | It's nothing, really. | Ask me later.

rule s8d_ans_any3
does answer.detail
asserts none
say Who can say? | You've got me there. | Not sure, to be honest. | I'd have to think on that. | Ah, that'd be telling.

# Who says it: #s8_evade# (plain.grammar), the speaker's own way of not quite answering (the merry tease, the cold
# shut it, a pup doesn't know), the most specific that holds; these rules rank with the three above.
rule s8d_ans_who
does answer.detail
asserts none
say #s8_evade# | #s8_evade# | #s8_evade# | Not sure, I'm afraid.

rule s8d_ans_who2
does answer.detail
asserts none
say #s8_evade# | #s8_evade# | Well, you know how it is. | Ah. That's a long story.

rule s8d_ans_work
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=work|day
say Oh, this and that. | The usual. | Same as ever. | Enough to keep me busy. | Nothing worth the telling.

rule s8d_ans_work_working
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=work|day self.working=yes
say Busy enough. | Run off my feet. | There's always more.

rule s8d_ans_work_none
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=work|day self.job=none
say Not much, these days. | I'm between things. | Whatever comes along.

rule s8d_ans_home
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=home|family|food
say Oh, the usual. | Not mine, I'll tell you that. | Same as always. | Don't ask.

rule s8d_ans_health
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=health
tone tender
say It comes and goes. | I'll live. | Better than it was. | Don't fuss.

rule s8d_ans_travel
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=travel|accent|land
say A fair way off. | Far enough. | Not so far, really. | You'd not find it on your own.

rule s8d_ans_travel_away
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=travel|accent self.from!=ridgemere
say Where I grew up. | Back home, that is. | Where I'm from.

rule s8d_ans_story
does answer.detail
asserts none
when conv.topic=memories|lore|dreams|pastimes|animals|friends|faith|season|weather|smalltalk
say That's the end of it. | Nothing, after that. | That's all there was. | That's the whole tale.

## A traveller standing near (the player topic: topic.subject, a name the speaker was given or how they look; their
## pronoun by sex). Asked about, and what can be said: nothing the town doesn't know.

rule s8d_ask_player
does ask.detail
when conv.topic=player|deed
say Where's #topic.they# from, do you think? | What's #topic.they# after, here? | Staying long, is #topic.they#? | Has #topic.they# said anything to you?

rule s8d_ans_player
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=player|deed
say Ask #topic.them# yourself. | Couldn't tell you. Travellers keep their own counsel. | Not a word to me. | Who knows, with travellers.

rule s8d_ans_player_known
does answer.detail
when conv.topic=player topic.known=yes
say I've spoken with #topic.them# once or twice. That's all. | We've talked. Pleasant enough. | I know #topic.them# to nod to.
